    "expectedRule": "Chapter 17 pairs each evidence with a trap (residue_evidence with residue_sterility_trap). Entering an evidence node needs its trap cleared and leaving it needs the evidence revealed (`先揭示当前证据再离开。`). A trap that damages the player before its evidence is revealed contaminates that evidence (no custody_shell here); countering it with its item deals no damage and contaminates nothing. Collecting an evidence reveals it; a clean revealed evidence is trusted and eliminates its suspect (residue -> records_keeper). Entering verdict_chamber needs one revealed evidence (`至少揭示一份证据后开放。`); its first clear leaves a pending verdict that blocks leaving with `原始裁决尚未完成，请先选择指控对象。`. law/resolve-verdict accuses a suspect: correct only for route_surveyor, with the trusted count frozen at that moment; a second accusation changes nothing. The boss gate (verdict_chamber -> false_testimony_judge) needs a completed verdict. Selecting the boss freezes {suspect, correct, trustedCount, appealed, eliminatedSuspects}; in the boss encounter a wrong verdict gives enemy all stats +10% and outgoing force/art +10%, a correct one with 1-2 trusted evidence -4% and +8%. With mist_breathing as the main method the risked residue trap deals floor(205 x 0.45) = 92. The counter item comes from a prepared tactical loadout (one armor_patch). The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
  "baseInput": {
    "path": "packages/save-codec/tests/fixtures/new-hub-v1.json",
